<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hugh of Saint-Omer</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1106</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Hugh of Fauquembergues</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hugh of Saint-Omer, also called Hugh of Fauquembergues, was a knight from Artois who came east with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-crusade">First Crusade</a>. In 1101, when Tancred left for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a>, King Baldwin I gave him the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galilee">Galilee</a>. Around 1105 he built the castle of Toron at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibnin">Tibnin</a> in the hills above <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyre">Tyre</a> to support raids on the city. He was killed in 1106 fighting a force from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hugh-of-saint-omer.jpg" alt="Hugh of Saint-Omer" width="320" height="321" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hugues_II_de_Saint-Omer.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
